X:1
T:The ayah's song
T:Hindostani song from the steamer (sketch)
C:traditional (North India)
O:India
R:air
S:Fox Strangways, The Music of Hindostan (1914), Ex. 160, p. 66
N:A SKETCH. Adagio, crotchet 80. One of three songs an ayah sang on board the steamer; Fox Strangways says she lost her key and the songs were hard to piece together, and that the slide to the close and the half-close gave them their value. The slide is written here as grace notes before the two cadence notes. The tune falls below the stave to A; sing it a fourth up. No words are printed. Every bar wants checking against the plate.
